// === PREAMBLE ===
// @trope    Rogue Juror
// @category Oratory / Persuasion
// @source   https://allthetropes.org/wiki/Rogue_Juror
// @version  1.3
// @domain    Narrative
//
// Laconic (per the wiki): the lone juror who holds out against the rest, refusing to convict while a
// doubt remains, and reasons the room around. FRONTIER: the BURDEN OF PROOF as a gate. Every
// persuasion rule so far flips belief on any sufficient appeal — there is no THRESHOLD. The
// courtroom adds one: to convict, the jury must be persuaded AND free of reasonable doubt, and the
// burden sits on the accuser. So a single raised doubt can DEFEAT an otherwise-persuasive case — the
// defensive mirror of persuasion, where not-believing is the disciplined act. The jury is the
// audience, deliberating with itself.

import "trl/modules/persuasion.trl"          // the jury is the audience; doubt tests the case

assoc rogue_juror -> [
  persuasion      : "imposes the burden of proof on",
  cassandra_truth : "is the disciplined cousin of (doubt withheld, not truth ignored)",
  common_knowledge : "turns one juror's doubt into the room's"
]

imply RogueJuror -> [Doubt, Judgment, Narrative]

// Naming rule: a reasonable doubt raised against a verdict the jury had been persuaded of unseats
// it — the standard, not the persuasion, decides. The burden was never on the doubter.
rule Reasonable_Doubt {
  when:
    audience [+Persuaded(of=$verdict)]
    evt $d [&Doubts(agent=$j, claim=$verdict)]
  then:
    audience [-Persuaded]
    audience [+Acquits]
    audience -- reasonable_doubt
}

// === CONCRETE VIGNETTE: Twelve Angry Men — Juror 8 (film, 1957) ===
// Eleven jurors are ready to convict in minutes; the prosecution's case felt airtight. Juror 8 does
// not claim the boy is innocent — only that he is not SURE, and that sure is what the law requires.
// The switchblade that is not unique, the old man who could not have heard, the woman who was not
// wearing her glasses: each is a doubt, and one reasonable doubt is enough.
char prosecutor [+Speaker] [+Credible]

scene the_deliberation {
  beat 1 {
    evt the_case    [&Argues(agent=prosecutor, thesis=guilty)]
    evt the_exhibit [&Cites(agent=prosecutor, support=the_switchblade)]
    // Establish_Ethos + Persuade_By_Logos -> audience [+Persuaded(of=guilty)]
  }
  beat 2 {
    evt juror_eight [&Doubts(agent=davis, claim=guilty)]
    // Reasonable_Doubt -> audience [-Persuaded] [+Acquits] -- reasonable_doubt
  }
}
